;k‰ΩJûˆ<)Û≤ªX%Ë<π/=Z·Û<ôB⁄<b‹Å<πŸ—º†ò˜;ÂO˚º˛|	ªâ‰9=IØÛªä∏<¢%={"title": "PER\u00cdODOS SUPERIORES A 16 SEMANAS:Los per\u00edodos superiores a 16 semanas se refieren a la duraci\u00f3n recomendada para el uso de dietas VLCD, que no se aconseja exceder."}{"title": "COMPOSICI\u00d3N:La composici\u00f3n se refiere a los nutrientes y calor\u00edas que contienen los productos de muy bajo contenido cal\u00f3rico."}{"title": "DURACI\u00d3N DE USO:La duraci\u00f3n de uso se refiere al tiempo recomendado para seguir una dieta VLCD, que no debe exceder 16 semanas."}{"title": "DIABETES TYPE 1:Diabetes Type 1 is an autoimmune medical condition characterized by the body's inability to produce insulin, leading to elevated blood glucose levels. This condition increases the risk of developing ketosis and hypoglycemia, especially in patients who are following a Very Low-Calorie Diet (VLCD). Additionally, Diabetes Type 1 has been associated with celiac disease, which is thought to be linked through shared genetic factors."}{"title": "ORNISH DIET:The Ornish Diet is a low-fat diet that emphasizes the reduction of fat intake and is designed for weight loss and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "PRITIKIN DIET:The Pritikin Diet is another low-fat dietary approach aimed at modifying lifestyle for the prevention of cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "GASTROINTESTINAL DISCOMFORT:Gastrointestinal discomfort is a common side effect associated with VLCD, including symptoms like nausea and constipation."}{"title": "AMERICAN ACADEMY OF FAMILY PHYSICIANS:The American Academy of Family Physicians is a professional organization that provides guidelines on dietary practices, including definitions of low-carbohydrate diets."}{"title": "DIETAS BAJAS EN HIDRATOS DE CARBONO:Low-carbohydrate diets (DBHC) are dietary plans that restrict carbohydrate intake and have gained popularity for weight loss and metabolic health."}{"title": "DIETA ATKINS:The Atkins Diet, known in Spanish as \"la dieta Atkins,\" is a low-carbohydrate diet that emphasizes high protein and fat intake while significantly limiting carbohydrate consumption. It is often classified as a hyperproteic diet and has gained popularity for its effectiveness in weight loss, frequently being referred to as a miracle diet. The diet's approach focuses on reducing carbohydrate intake to promote fat burning and weight loss, making it a well-known option for those seeking to manage their weight."}{"title": "SOUTH BEACH:The South Beach Diet is another popular low-carbohydrate diet that focuses on healthy fats and proteins while reducing carbohydrate intake."}{"title": "CETOG\u00c9NICAS:Ketogenic diets are a type of very low-carbohydrate diet that induces ketosis, mentioned in the context of low-carbohydrate diets."}{"title": "PERFIL LIP\u00cdDICO:Lipid profile refers to the levels of various types of fats in the blood, which can be affected by dietary choices, including low-carbohydrate diets."}{"title": "EFECTOS SECUNDARIOS:\"EFECTOS SECUNDARIOS\" refers to side effects that are a significant concern in the development of obesity treatments. These side effects can also be observed in other medical treatments, such as oncological therapies, where they manifest as symptoms like nausea and loss of appetite, which negatively impact the patient's nutrition. Additionally, side effects can arise from low-carbohydrate diets, leading to adverse reactions such as constipation and headaches. Overall, \"EFECTOS SECUNDARIOS\" encompasses a range of adverse reactions that can affect both obesity treatments and other medical interventions, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing these effects to ensure patient well-being."}{"title": "DBHC:DBHC refers to a type of diet that has been studied for its long-term safety and efficacy, particularly in relation to fat consumption and mortality rates."}{"title": "DBIG:DBIG refers to diets with a low glycemic index, which classify carbohydrates based on their impact on blood sugar levels."}{"title": "MONTIGNAC:Montignac is a popular figure associated with low glycemic index diets, known for promoting dietary methods that emphasize carbohydrate quality."}{"title": "SUGAR BUSTERS:Sugar Busters is a well-known diet plan that focuses on reducing sugar intake and promoting low glycemic index foods."}{"title": "PLATANO:Pl\u00e1tano is a fruit commonly known as bananas, recognized for its energy-boosting properties. It contains a fructose content ranging from 3 to 6 grams per 100 grams. Additionally, pl\u00e1tano has a glycemic index of 83, which indicates a significant impact on blood sugar levels."}{"title": "HELADO ITALIANO:Helado italiano refers to Italian ice cream, which has a glycemic index of 114, indicating its impact on blood sugar levels."}{"title": "ESPAGUETIS:Espaguetis refers to spaghetti, which has a glycemic index of 54 when cooked for 5 minutes and 83 when cooked for 10 minutes."}{"title": "COCA-COLA:"}{"title": "DIETA HIPERPROTEICA:La dieta hiperproteica se refiere a un tipo de dieta que tiene un alto contenido de prote\u00ednas, generalmente superior al 20-30% del aporte cal\u00f3rico total, y se ha popularizado por su potencial efecto en la p\u00e9rdida de peso."}{"title": "DIETA DE LA ZONA:La dieta de la Zona es un enfoque diet\u00e9tico que propone una proporci\u00f3n de nutrientes de 40% carbohidratos, 30% prote\u00ednas y 30% grasas, y se considera una dieta hiperproteica."}{"title": "ANTIOXIDANTES FEN\u00d3LICOS:Los antioxidantes fen\u00f3licos son compuestos que se derivan del consumo de fibra y que pueden ser reducidos por dietas bajas en carbohidratos, afectando la salud intestinal."}{"title": "CARNES BLANCAS:CARNES BLANCAS, which refers to white meats such as poultry and rabbit, are preferred in the Mediterranean diet over red and processed meats, contributing to a healthier eating pattern. These white meats are included in dietary guidelines that emphasize specific health considerations, highlighting their role in promoting overall well-being."}{"title": "CARNES ROJAS:CARNES ROJAS, or red meats, are consumed in lesser quantities within the Mediterranean diet, which is associated with various health benefits. Dietary guidelines discuss red meat consumption, highlighting its potential link to cancer and recommending moderation based on its health impacts. Additionally, red meats are identified as a significant source of saturated fats, which can impair renal excretion of urate, leading to elevated uric acid levels. Overall, the consumption of red meats is approached with caution in dietary recommendations due to these health considerations."}{"title": "L\u00c1CTEOS:L\u00e1cteos, or dairy products, encompass a variety of food items derived from milk, including milk, cheese, and yogurt. These products are recognized for their high-quality proteins and essential nutrients, particularly calcium, which are crucial for children's growth and development. Dietary guidelines recommend the inclusion of dairy products in children's diets due to their health benefits. However, it is noted that the consumption of dairy is relatively low in the Mediterranean diet, which may contribute to certain health risks.\n\nIn terms of dietary recommendations, it is advised that dairy products be consumed in controlled portions, with a limit of two servings per day suggested before medical tests. Additionally, it is important to avoid commercial dairy preparations that may contain gluten. Low-fat dairy products, in particular, have been associated with lower uric acid levels and a reduced risk of hyperuricemia. Overall, while dairy products are beneficial, moderation and careful selection are emphasized to maximize their health benefits."}{"title": "AZ\u00daCARES A\u00d1ADIDOS:La dieta mediterr\u00e1nea se caracteriza por un bajo consumo de az\u00facares a\u00f1adidos, lo que puede ayudar a prevenir enfermedades metab\u00f3licas."}{"title": "AGENCIA ESPA\u00d1OLA DE SEGURIDAD ALIMENTARIA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The AGENCIA ESPA\u00d1OLA DE SEGURIDAD ALIMENTARIA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N (AESAN) is the Spanish agency tasked with overseeing food safety and nutrition policies in Spain. It is responsible for providing guidelines on various dietary practices, including miracle diets, and their potential implications for health. AESAN plays a crucial role in ensuring that food safety standards are met and that the nutritional needs of the population are addressed effectively."}{"title": "PACIENTE OBESO:An obese patient is an individual who may require bariatric surgery and needs a structured nutritional education program for healthy eating habits."}{"title": "CL\u00cdNICA MAYO:Cl\u00ednica Mayo, also known as Mayo Clinic, is a prominent medical institution recognized for its extensive research and innovative treatment protocols. Among its notable contributions to medical science is the MELD score, a critical tool used for assessing liver disease severity. In addition to its medical research, Cl\u00ednica Mayo offers a variety of dietary programs, some of which are categorized as miracle diets, reflecting its commitment to holistic health and wellness."}{"title": "DIETA DE HAY:The Hay Diet is a disassociative diet that separates food types to aid in weight loss, often categorized as a miracle diet."}{"title": "DIETA HOLLYWOOD:The Hollywood Diet is a popular diet that promises quick weight loss, often considered a miracle diet."}{"title": "DIETA DUKAN:The Dukan Diet is a high-protein diet that claims to promote rapid weight loss, categorized as a miracle diet."}{"title": "DIETAS MILAGRO:\"DIETAS MILAGRO\" refers to miracle diets, which are weight loss plans that claim to deliver rapid results. However, these diets often lack scientific backing and may pose various health risks to individuals who follow them."}{"title": "SEMISOLID DIET:The \"SEMISOLID DIET\" is a dietary phase that follows the liquid diet, primarily designed for individuals transitioning back to solid foods. This phase consists of pureed or mashed foods, allowing for a gradual reintroduction of more solid textures. It is particularly relevant for patients who have undergone bariatric surgery, as it serves as a transitional stage where they can safely incorporate pur\u00e9es and soft foods into their diet. The semisolid diet plays a crucial role in helping individuals adjust their eating habits while ensuring proper nutrition during recovery."}{"title": "NORMAL CONSISTENCY DIET:The \"NORMAL CONSISTENCY DIET\" is the final phase following bariatric surgery, designed for patients to gradually reintroduce a variety of foods into their diet. During this phase, individuals are encouraged to focus on nutritional balance while consuming easily digestible solid foods. This diet allows for a broader range of food options, supporting the transition to a more typical eating pattern while still prioritizing the health and nutritional needs of the patient."}{"title": "TRIGLYCERIDES DE CADENA MEDIA (MCT):MCTs are a type of fat that may be beneficial in the diet post-bariatric surgery due to their unique metabolic properties."}{"title": "TRIGLYCERIDES DE CADENA LARGA (LCT):LCTs are a type of fat that are more calorically dense and may be less favorable in the post-bariatric surgery diet."}{"title": "NHANES III:NHANES III is a series of studies designed to assess the health and nutritional status of adults and children in the United States."}{"title": "CARDIA:CARDIA is a long-term study that investigates the development of cardiovascular disease in young adults."}{"title": "HERITAGE FAMILY STUDY:HERITAGE Family Study is a research project that examines the role of genetics in physical fitness and health."}{"title": "GLUCOMANANO:Glucomanano is a dietary fiber supplement that is used for weight loss and cholesterol management."}{"title": "SALAS-SALVAD\u00d3:Anna Salas-Salvad\u00f3 is an esteemed author in the field of nutrition and dietetics, recognized for her significant contributions to clinical nutrition literature. She is notably a co-author of nutritional recommendations aimed at the prevention and treatment of obesity, highlighting her expertise and commitment to addressing this critical health issue."}{"title": "BARBANY:Barbany is a contributor to the consensus on the evaluation and intervention of obesity published in Rev Esp Obes."}{"title": "ARANCETA J:Aranceta J is a co-author of the guidelines for the treatment of obesity."}{"title": "BELLIDO D:Bellido D is a contributor to the clinical practice guidelines for obesity management."}{"title": "GARVEY WT:Garvey WT is a researcher who has made significant contributions to clinical practice guidelines for obesity management. In addition to this role, Garvey WT serves as a reviewer for the AACE/ACE Obesity Clinical Practice Guidelines, further demonstrating their expertise and involvement in the field of obesity research and clinical practice."}{"title": "MECHANICK JI:Mechanick JI is a researcher actively engaged in the development of obesity management guidelines. In addition to this role, Mechanick JI serves as a reviewer for the AACE/ACE guidelines pertaining to obesity management, contributing expertise to ensure the guidelines are comprehensive and effective."}{"title": "BRETT EM:Brett EM is a researcher actively involved in studies focused on obesity treatment. In addition to his research contributions, he serves as a reviewer for the AACE/ACE guidelines pertaining to obesity management, indicating his expertise and influence in the field."}{"title": "HURLEY DL:Hurley DL is a researcher actively involved in studies focused on obesity treatment. In addition to their research contributions, Hurley DL also serves as a reviewer for the AACE/ACE guidelines pertaining to obesity management, indicating a significant role in shaping clinical practices in this field."}{"title": "JASTREBOFF AM:Jastreboff AM is a researcher actively engaged in the development of obesity management guidelines. In addition to their research contributions, Jastreboff AM serves as a reviewer for the AACE/ACE guidelines pertaining to obesity management, further emphasizing their expertise and involvement in this critical area of health."}{"title": "GREEN MA:Green MA is a researcher who conducted a cluster analysis exploring subgroups of the obese."}{"title": "STRONG M:Strong M is a researcher involved in the study of obesity subgroups."}{"title": "RAZAK F:Razak F is a researcher who contributed to the analysis of obesity subgroups."}{"title": "SUBRAMANIAN SV:Subramanian SV is a researcher involved in the study of obesity subgroups."}{"title": "REVIEWERS OF AACE/ACE:The reviewers of the AACE/ACE guidelines are a group of experts who evaluate clinical practices for obesity management."}{"title": "J PUBLIC HEALTH:J Public Health is a journal that published research on obesity subgroups."}{"title": "N ENGLAND JOURNAL OF MEDICINE:The New England Journal of Medicine is a prestigious medical journal recognized for its contributions to the field of medicine. It publishes a wide range of research and reviews on various medical topics, including significant issues such as the complications associated with central venous catheterization. Additionally, the journal has featured studies that explore dietary impacts on health, including a notable study that compared the effects of low-carbohydrate and low-fat diets in individuals with severe obesity. Through its rigorous publication standards, the New England Journal of Medicine plays a vital role in disseminating important medical knowledge and research findings."}{"title": "INT J OBESITY:The International Journal of Obesity published a meta-analysis on weight management using meal replacement strategies."}{"title": "COCHRANE DATABASE:The Cochrane Database is a comprehensive collection of databases in the fields of medicine and other healthcare specialties, primarily focused on providing high-quality, independent evidence to inform healthcare decision-making. It contains systematic reviews and meta-analyses that offer evidence-based information on various healthcare interventions. Among its extensive resources, the Cochrane Database includes systematic reviews that specifically address interventions for conditions such as cystic fibrosis, as well as published reviews on topics like low glycemic index diets for managing overweight and obesity. Overall, the Cochrane Database serves as a vital tool for healthcare professionals seeking reliable evidence to guide their clinical practices."}{"title": "PUBLIC HEALTH NUTRITION:Public Health Nutrition is a journal that published research on energy-restricted diets and insulin sensitivity."}{"title": "REV ESP OBES:Rev Esp Obes is a journal that published various studies and recommendations related to obesity."}{"title": "MINISTERIO DE SANIDAD, POL\u00cdTICA SOCIAL E IGUALDAD:The Ministry of Health, Social Policy and Equality is a governmental organization in Spain responsible for public health and social policies."}{"title": "CENTRO DE SALUD LUCERO:Centro de Salud Lucero is a primary healthcare center located in Madrid, dedicated to providing essential health services to the community. This facility, also referred to as the Lucero Health Center, plays a vital role in delivering medical services to the residents of the area, ensuring accessible healthcare for all."}{"title": "CARMEN MORENO LOPERA:Carmen Moreno Lopera is a healthcare professional working in primary care at the Lucero Health Center in Madrid."}{"title": "F\u00c1RMACOS COMERCIALIZADOS:Marketed drugs refer to pharmaceutical products that are available for sale and used in the treatment of various conditions, including obesity."}{"title": "FUTURO DE LOS TRATAMIENTOS PARA LA OBESIDAD:The future of obesity treatments involves ongoing research and development of new therapies and interventions to manage obesity effectively."}{"title": "LORCASERINA:Lorcaserina is a serotonin receptor agonist that has been approved by the FDA for the treatment of obesity. However, it was rejected by the European Medicines Agency (EMA) due to safety concerns. This weight loss medication is often discussed alongside other central action drugs, such as fentermina and topiramato, highlighting its role in the pharmacological landscape of obesity treatment."}{"title": "FENTERMINE:Fentermina is a medication primarily used in combination with topiramate for the treatment of obesity. It is a noradrenergic agent that has been approved by the FDA for appetite reduction in individuals struggling with obesity. Fentermina was initially marketed in 1956, highlighting its long-standing presence in the pharmacological landscape. However, it is important to note that while it has received FDA approval, it has not been approved by the European Medicines Agency (EMA)."}{"title": "BLOSSOM:The BLOSSOM study is a clinical trial designed to evaluate the effectiveness, efficacy, and tolerability of lorcaserin for obesity management. This study involves a total of 4,008 subjects and spans a duration of 52 weeks."}{"title": "AMINOREX:Aminorex was a weight loss drug introduced in 1965 but was withdrawn in 1968 due to hypertension pulmonary risks."}{"title": "MAZINDOL:Mazindol was a weight loss medication introduced in 1970 and suspended in 1993 in Australia due to safety concerns."}{"title": "FENFLURAMINA:Fenfluramina was a weight loss drug approved in Europe in 1963 and in the US in 1973, withdrawn due to cardiac valve disease and pulmonary hypertension risks."}{"title": "DEXFENFLURAMINA:Dexfenfluramina was introduced in 1985 in Europe and 1996 in the US but was withdrawn due to risks of cardiac valve disease and pulmonary hypertension."}{"title": "SIBUTRAMINA:Sibutramina is a weight loss medication that was approved in the United States in 1997 and in Europe in 2001. It has been compared to other weight loss drugs, such as fentermina and topiramato, particularly regarding patient abandonment rates. However, due to concerns over cardiovascular risks, Sibutramina was withdrawn from the market in 2010."}{"title": "RIMONABANT:Rimonabant was approved in Europe in 2006 for obesity treatment but was withdrawn in 2009 due to severe psychiatric side effects."}{"title": "DINITROFENOL:"}{"title": "BLOOM:The BLOOM study is a clinical trial assessing the effects of lorcaserin on overweight and obesity management, with 3182 patients over 2 years."}{"title": "BLOOM-DM:The BLOOM-DM study is a clinical trial focused on the effects of lorcaserin for obesity management in patients with diabetes, involving 604 patients."}{"title": "LORCASERIN:Lorcaserin is a medication used for weight management, approved by the FDA in 2012, with a modest efficacy profile and various side effects."}{"title": "TOPIRAMATE:Topiramate is a medication approved for partial seizures and migraine prophylaxis, which is used in combination with fentermina for obesity treatment."}{"title": "QSYMIAR:Qsymia is a combination medication of fentermina and topiramate approved by the FDA in 2012 for obesity treatment."}{"title": "SEROTONIN:Serotonin is a neurotransmitter involved in mood regulation, which is mentioned in relation to the effects of lorcaserin and its potential side effects."}{"title": "CARCINOGENICITY:Carcinogenicity refers to the potential of a substance to cause cancer, which is a concern raised regarding lorcaserin based on animal studies."}{"title": "NAUSEA:Nausea is a common side effect experienced by subjects taking liraglutida, as reported in clinical trials. Additionally, it is also one of the significant side effects reported in studies involving lorcaserin and its combinations. This indicates that nausea is a notable adverse effect associated with both liraglutida and lorcaserin, highlighting its prevalence in clinical settings related to these medications."}{"title": "HEADACHES:Headaches are a common side effect associated with the use of lorcaserin and its combinations in obesity treatment."}{"title": "DIZZINESS:Dizziness is another side effect reported in the studies involving lorcaserin and its combinations."}{"title": "ASTHENIA:Asthenia, or weakness, is a side effect noted in the context of lorcaserin treatment."}{"title": "CONSTIPATION:Constipation is a side effect associated with the use of lorcaserin in obesity management."}{"title": "DRY MOUTH:Dry mouth is a side effect reported in the studies involving lorcaserin and its combinations."}{"title": "SYNDROME SEROTONINERGICO:Serotonin syndrome is a potentially life-threatening condition that can occur with certain medications, mentioned as a contraindication for lorcaserin."}{"title": "SYNDROME NEUROL\u00c9PTICO MALIGNO:Neuroleptic malignant syndrome is a severe reaction to antipsychotic medications, mentioned as a contraindication for lorcaserin."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD RENAL CR\u00d3NICA AVANZADA:Advanced chronic kidney disease is identified as a contraindication for the use of lorcaserin. This condition, referred to as \"ENFERMEDAD RENAL CR\u00d3NICA AVANZADA,\" indicates a severe decline in kidney function, which may pose risks when using certain medications like lorcaserin."}{"title": "VALVULOPAT\u00cdAS:Valvulopathies refer to diseases of the heart valves, which are mentioned as a precaution for lorcaserin use."}{"title": "BRADICARDIA:Bradycardia, or slow heart rate, is mentioned as a precaution for the use of lorcaserin."}{"title": "EQUIP:EQUIP is a phase III randomized controlled trial that evaluates the combination of controlled-release phentermine and topiramate for the treatment of obesity in severely obese adults. The trial specifically studies the effects of this combination therapy, aiming to assess its efficacy and safety in managing obesity."}{"title": "FENTERMINA:Fentermina is a medication used for weight loss, often combined with topiramate to enhance its effects."}{"title": "CONQUER:CONQUER is a randomized, placebo-controlled, phase 3 trial that investigates the effects of low-dose, controlled-release phentermine, also referred to as fentermina, in combination with topiramate. The study focuses on weight management and the associated comorbidities in overweight and obese adults. Through its design, CONQUER aims to provide insights into the efficacy of this medication regimen for improving health outcomes related to obesity."}{"title": "SEQUEL:SEQUEL is a randomized, placebo-controlled, phase 3 extension study that focuses on sustained weight loss and metabolic benefits associated with controlled-release phentermine/topiramate. This study serves as an extension of the CONQUER trial, continuing to follow participants for a duration of two years."}{"title": "NALTREXONA/BUPROPION:Naltrexona/bupropion is a combination medication for weight loss that is also compared to fentermina and topiramato."}{"title": "GLAUCOMA:Glaucoma is a medical condition that is listed as a contraindication for the use of fentermina and topiramato."}{"title": "TAQUIARRITMIAS:Taquiarritmias are a type of heart rhythm disorder that is mentioned as a precaution for patients using fentermina and topiramato."}{"title": "ACIDOSIS HIPERCLOR\u00c9MICA:Acidosis hiperclor\u00e9mica is a medical condition that is mentioned as a precaution for the use of fentermina and topiramato."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES HEP\u00c1TICAS:Alteraciones hep\u00e1ticas refers to liver disorders that encompass a range of liver abnormalities. These disorders are significant as they serve as a precaution for the use of certain medications, specifically fentermina and topiramato. Additionally, in pediatric patients receiving parenteral nutrition, alteraciones hep\u00e1ticas can manifest as elevated liver enzymes and cholestasis, highlighting the importance of monitoring liver function in these individuals."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES COGNITIVAS:Alteraciones cognitivas refers to cognitive impairments that may occur with the use of fentermina and topiramato, especially when combined with other substances."}{"title": "ANTICONCEPTIVOS:Anticonceptivos are birth control medications that may interact with fentermina and topiramato, affecting menstrual cycles."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS DEPRESIVOS:S\u00edntomas depresivos refers to depressive symptoms that may occur in patients taking fentermina and topiramato.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "XENDOS:XENDOS is a randomized double-blind study involving 3,305 non-diabetic obese patients, aimed at evaluating the effectiveness of the weight loss drug Xenical in preventing diabetes. The study specifically focuses on the prevention of diabetes among obese individuals through the administration of this medication."}{"title": "CONTRAVE:Contrave is a combination medication of bupropion and naltrexone approved in the USA for weight management."}{"title": "MYSIMBA:Mysimba is the European name for the combination of bupropion and naltrexone used for weight management."}{"title": "COR:COR refers to the Contrave Obesity Research studies that evaluated the effectiveness of the bupropion-naltrexone combination in obese patients."}{"title": "COR-BMOD:COR-BMOD is a study designed to evaluate the effects of intensive lifestyle changes in conjunction with a combination therapy of bupropion and naltrexone on weight loss. This trial specifically investigates the impact of naltrexone SR and bupropion SR as adjuncts to behavior modification, aiming to enhance weight loss outcomes through a comprehensive approach that includes both pharmacological and behavioral interventions."}{"title": "PACIENTES CON SOBREPESO Y OBESIDAD:Patients with overweight and obesity were the subjects of the studies evaluating the effectiveness of bupropion and naltrexone."}{"title": "COLELITIASIS:Cholelithiasis, also known as colelitiasis, is the presence of gallstones in the gallbladder. This condition is significant as it necessitates caution for patients who are taking weight loss medications and certain other drugs. The presence of gallstones can lead to complications, making it important for healthcare providers to monitor and manage patients with this condition carefully."}{"title": "WARFARINA:Warfarina is an anticoagulant medication that plays a crucial role in preventing blood clots. It is important to note that Warfarina may interact with weight loss medications, necessitating careful monitoring of patients who are using both. Additionally, the efficacy of Warfarina can be significantly influenced by dietary factors, particularly vitamin K intake, which may counteract its anticoagulant effects. Furthermore, the absorption of Warfarina can be altered by enteral nutrition, potentially impacting its therapeutic action. Certain foods, especially those high in fat, can also decrease the effectiveness of Warfarina. Therefore, patients on Warfarina should be aware of these interactions and dietary considerations to ensure optimal therapeutic outcomes."}{"title": "BN:BN is a pharmaceutical treatment that reduces blood pressure and is involved in cardiovascular safety studies."}{"title": "LIGHT STUDY:The LIGHT study is a cardiovascular safety study initiated by the FDA to evaluate the safety of BN."}{"title": "DPP-IV:Dipeptidyl peptidase-IV (DPP-IV) is an enzyme that degrades GLP-1, and liraglutida is resistant to its action."}{"title": "2022:2022 is the year when definitive results from the new cardiovascular safety study for BN are expected."}{"title": "ANOREXIA NERVOSA:Anorexia Nervosa (AN) is a serious psychological condition and a specific type of restrictive eating disorder characterized by an intense fear of gaining weight and a distorted body image. This disorder leads individuals to significantly restrict their food intake, resulting in severe weight loss and various health complications. The intense fear of weight gain and the distorted perception of body image are central to the condition, making it a complex and challenging disorder to treat. Anorexia Nervosa is contraindicated for the use of certain treatments, such as BN, highlighting the need for specialized care in managing this serious eating disorder."}{"title": "BIPOLAR DISORDER:Bipolar disorder is a mental health condition that requires special attention when using BN."}{"title": "EPILEPSY:Epilepsy is a neurological disorder characterized by recurrent seizures. It may be precipitated by the use of certain substances, such as BN, particularly in patients who are on anticomicial drugs. In addition to traditional medical treatments, dietary therapies, including the ketogenic diet, are being explored as potential treatments for managing epilepsy."}{"title": "CARDIOVASCULAR EVENTS:Cardiovascular events include serious health incidents like heart attack or stroke, which are monitored in studies like LIGHT."}{"title": "ANXIETY DISORDER:Generalized anxiety disorder is a mental health condition that requires caution when using BN."}{"title": "FATIGUE:Fatigue is a potential side effect of BN treatment that may affect patients."}{"title": "SAXENDA:Saxenda is a brand name for liraglutida at a higher dosage, specifically developed for weight management."}{"title": "SCALE:SCALE refers to a series of clinical trials conducted to evaluate the efficacy and safety of liraglutida in various patient groups with obesity."}{"title": "CART:CART (Cocaine and Amphetamine-Regulated Transcript) is a neuropeptide that plays a role in the regulation of appetite and energy homeostasis."}{"title": "NEUROP\u00c9PTIDO-Y:Neuropeptide Y is a peptide that is involved in regulating energy balance, appetite, and stress response."}{"title": "AGRP:AGRP (Agouti-Related Peptide) is a neuropeptide that stimulates appetite and is involved in energy homeostasis."}{"title": "GABA:GABA, or Gamma-Aminobutyric Acid, is an organic molecule that functions as a neurotransmitter in the brain. It plays a crucial role in inhibiting nerve transmission, which is essential for regulating various physiological processes, including appetite. Additionally, GABA is involved in the brain's defense mechanisms against cerebral edema, particularly during conditions of hyponatremia. Through its inhibitory effects, GABA contributes to maintaining the balance of excitatory and inhibitory signals in the nervous system, thereby supporting overall brain health and function."}{"title": "N\u00daCLEOS HIPOTAL\u00c1MICOS:N\u00facleos hipotal\u00e1micos refers to the hypothalamic nuclei that are involved in the regulation of hunger and satiety."}{"title": "SCALE STUDIES:The SCALE studies are clinical trials that evaluate the effectiveness of liraglutida in weight loss and its impact on various health conditions."}{"title": "SAHS:SAHS refers to the syndrome of sleep apnea-hypopneas, a condition studied in relation to liraglutida's effects on weight loss."}{"title": "PLACEBO:Placebo is a control treatment used in clinical trials to compare the effects of liraglutida against no active medication."}{"title": "VOMITING:Vomiting is another side effect noted in subjects taking liraglutida, occurring in a smaller proportion of participants."}{"title": "CARDIOVASCULAR RISK:Cardiovascular risk encompasses the likelihood of experiencing heart-related health issues, which is influenced by various factors, including diet and lifestyle choices. In particular, cardiovascular risk markers are evaluated in relation to the effects of liraglutide, especially among diabetic patients. This evaluation highlights the importance of understanding how dietary patterns and food choices can impact cardiovascular health. Overall, cardiovascular risk is a multifaceted concept that integrates the effects of individual health behaviors and medical treatments on the potential for developing cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "SUBJECTS:"}{"title": "FEN/TPM:FEN/TPM is a combination of drugs that is considered the most effective for weight loss based on clinical trial results."}{"title": "JAPAN:Japan is the country where cetilistat, a drug similar to orlistat, is approved for use."}{"title": "CETILISTAT:Cetilistat is a pharmaceutical treatment designed for obesity management, functioning as a gastric and pancreatic lipase inhibitor. It has been successfully tested in randomized controlled trials, demonstrating its efficacy in reducing body weight. Notably, cetilistat is associated with fewer side effects compared to orlistat, making it a potentially safer alternative for individuals seeking obesity treatment."}{"title": "TESOFENSINA:Tesofensina is a drug used for treating Parkinson's disease that has shown potential for weight loss in clinical trials."}{"title": "BELORANIF:Beloranif is a drug that inhibits MetAP2, reducing fat biosynthesis and increasing fat oxidation, showing significant weight loss in trials."}{"title": "BUPROPION-ZONISAMIDA:Bupropion-zonisamida is a drug combination being tested for obesity treatment."}{"title": "FENTERMINA-LORCASERINA:Fentermina-lorcaserina is another drug combination being tested for obesity treatment."}{"title": "GLP1:GLP1 is a hormone involved in the dual or triagonist agonists for gastrointestinal hormones that are being prioritized in obesity treatment."}{"title": "OBESITY SOCIETY:The Obesity Society is a professional organization dedicated to the study and treatment of obesity. It plays a significant role in advancing the understanding of obesity and has contributed to the development of guidelines for managing this condition. Through its efforts, the organization aims to improve the health and well-being of individuals affected by obesity."}{"title": "PARKINSON:Parkinson refers to Parkinson's disease, a progressive neurological disorder that primarily affects movement. This condition is characterized by symptoms such as tremors and stiffness. Additionally, it is noted that Parkinson's disease significantly impacts a considerable percentage of patients, leading to complications such as dysphagia (difficulty swallowing) and malnutrition."}{"title": "COLECISTITIS:Colecistitis is the inflammation of the gallbladder, noted in the context of drug precautions."}{"title": "ENSAYOS CL\u00cdNICOS:\"ENSAYOS CL\u00cdNICOS\" refers to clinical trials, which are research studies designed to evaluate the effects and safety of medications and medical approaches in human subjects. These trials are regulated by specific legislation and are essential for testing the efficacy of new treatments. They encompass a variety of focuses, including the effectiveness and safety of enteral nutrition products. Recent randomized clinical trials have demonstrated the efficacy of the ketogenic diet in treating epilepsy. Additionally, clinical trials are also conducted to assess treatments for gluten sensitivity and irritable bowel syndrome, highlighting their role in advancing medical knowledge and improving patient care."}{"title": "NORADRENALINA:Noradrenalina, also known as norepinephrine, is a hormone and neurotransmitter that plays a significant role in various physiological processes. It can increase in response to a low-sodium diet, which may impact sleep and other bodily functions. Additionally, noradrenalina is involved in the mechanism of action of tesofensina, indicating its importance in both hormonal regulation and neurotransmission."}{"title": "METAP2:MetAP2 is an enzyme that beloranif inhibits to reduce fat biosynthesis."}{"title": "FARMACOS DUAL Y TRIAGONISTAS:Dual and triagonist drugs are being developed for obesity treatment, targeting multiple hormonal pathways."}{"title": "FARMACOS CON MECANISMOS DE ACCION DIVERSOS:Drugs with diverse mechanisms of action are being combined to enhance obesity treatment efficacy.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "J AM COLL CARDIOL:The Journal of the American College of Cardiology publishes research related to cardiovascular disease and treatments."}{"title": "MIDDLETON KM:Middleton KM is a researcher who has contributed to studies on weight loss and obesity management."}{"title": "PATRIDAR SM:Patidar SM is a researcher involved in the systematic review and meta-analysis of weight loss maintenance."}{"title": "PERRI MG:Perri MG is a researcher who has studied the long-term maintenance of weight loss."}{"title": "KRENTZ AJ:Krentz AJ is a researcher focusing on pharmacological treatments for obesity."}{"title": "FUJIOKA K:Fujioka K is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of obesity treatment studies. Their work has enhanced the understanding of various obesity treatments, including their effectiveness and potential side effects."}{"title": "HOMPESCH M:Hompesch M is a researcher involved in the evolution of pharmacological treatments for obesity."}{"title": "CABRERIZO-GARC\u00cdA L:Cabrerizo-Garc\u00eda L is a researcher who has updated the pharmacology of obesity treatments."}{"title": "RUBIO-HERRERA MA:Rubio-Herrera MA is a researcher contributing to the pharmacological management of obesity."}{"title": "APOVIAN CM:Apovian CM is a prominent researcher and author specializing in clinical practice guidelines for obesity management. In addition to their contributions to clinical guidelines, Apovian CM is actively involved in the COR-II Study Group, which conducted a randomized, phase 3 trial investigating the effects of naltrexone SR/bupropion SR on weight and obesity-related risk factors. Through these efforts, Apovian CM plays a significant role in advancing the understanding and treatment of obesity."}{"title": "ARONNE LJ:Aronne LJ is a researcher involved in the pharmacological management of obesity."}{"title": "BESSEN DH:Bessen DH is a researcher who has contributed to obesity management studies."}{"title": "MCDONNELL ME:McDonnell ME is a researcher involved in obesity pharmacotherapy."}{"title": "PAGOTTO U:Pagotto U is a researcher contributing to the understanding of obesity treatments."}{"title": "BLOSSOM CLINICAL TRIAL GROUP:The BLOSSOM Clinical Trial Group conducted a trial on lorcaserin for weight loss in obese and overweight adults."}{"title": "SMITH SR:Smith SR is a researcher involved in multiple studies on obesity treatments."}{"title": "WEISSMAN NJ:Weissman NJ is a researcher who has contributed to obesity management studies."}{"title": "FIDLER MC:Fidler MC is a researcher involved in the BLOSSOM trial for weight loss."}{"title": "RAETHER B:Raether B is a researcher contributing to obesity treatment studies."}{"title": "SHANAHAN WR:Shanahan WR is a researcher involved in clinical trials for obesity treatments."}{"title": "ANDERSON CM:Anderson CM is a researcher who has contributed to studies on obesity management."}{"title": "O'NEIL PM:O'Neil PM is a researcher actively engaged in clinical trials focused on weight loss for individuals with type 2 diabetes. Additionally, O'Neil PM is involved in studies aimed at treating obesity, highlighting a commitment to addressing both diabetes and obesity through research initiatives."}{"title": "ZHANG J:Zhang J is a researcher contributing to obesity treatment studies."}{"title": "KHERAR:Khera R is a researcher who has studied pharmacological treatments for obesity."}{"title": "CHANDAR AK:Chandar AK is a researcher contributing to obesity treatment studies."}{"title": "DULAI PS:Dulai PS is a researcher involved in studies on obesity management."}{"title": "PROKOP LJ:Prokop LJ is a researcher involved in systematic reviews of obesity treatments."}{"title": "GADDE KM:Gadde KM is a researcher involved in obesity treatment studies."}{"title": "PETERSON CA:Peterson CA is a researcher contributing to obesity management studies."}{"title": "SCHWIERS ML:Schwiers ML is a researcher involved in obesity treatment studies."}{"title": "NAJARIAN T:Najarian T is a researcher contributing to obesity management studies."}{"title": "TROUPIN B:Troupin B is a researcher involved in obesity treatment studies."}{"title": "DAY WW:Day WW is a researcher contributing to obesity management studies."}{"title": "RUCKER D:Rucker D is a researcher who has studied long-term pharmacotherapy for obesity."}{"title": "PADWAL R:Padwal R is a researcher contributing to obesity treatment studies."}{"title": "LI SK:Li SK is a researcher involved in obesity management studies."}{"title": "CURIANI C:Curioni C is a researcher contributing to obesity treatment studies."}{"title": "LAU DCW:Lau DCW is a researcher involved in obesity management studies."}{"title": "TORGERSON JS:Torgerson JS is a researcher who has studied obesity treatments."}{"title": "HAUPTMAN J:Hauptman J is a researcher contributing to obesity treatment studies."}{"title": "BOLDRIN MN:Boldrin MN is a researcher involved in obesity management studies."}{"title": "ANDERSON JW:Anderson JW is a researcher involved in obesity management studies."}{"title": "GREENWAY FL:Greenway FL is a researcher who has studied pharmacotherapy for obesity."}{"title": "MCKENNEY J:McKenney J is a researcher contributing to obesity management studies."}{"title": "BUPROPION SR:Bupropion SR is a medication studied for its effects on weight loss."}{"title": "NALTREXONE PLUS BUPROPION:Naltrexone plus bupropion is a combination treatment studied for weight loss."}{"title": "EQUIP<(\"ENTITY\":EVENT"}{"title": "COR-I:COR-I is a multicenter, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 3 clinical trial designed to study the effects of naltrexone combined with bupropion on weight loss in overweight and obese adults. The trial specifically investigates the efficacy of bupropion, alongside naltrexone, in promoting weight loss in this population."}{"title": "COR-II:COR-II is a randomized, phase 3 trial designed to investigate the effects of naltrexone SR (sustained release) and bupropion SR on weight management and obesity-related risk factors. The trial aims to assess the efficacy of this combination treatment in promoting weight loss and improving associated health risks."}{"title": "OBESITY REV:Obesity Reviews is a journal that publishes systematic reviews and meta-analyses on obesity treatments and management."}{"title": "DIABETES OBES METABOL:Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism is a journal that focuses on the relationship between diabetes and obesity, including pharmacological treatments."}{"title": "UPROPION:Upropion is a medication studied for its effects on weight loss in overweight and obese adults through a multicentre, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 3 trial."}{"title": "HOLLANDER P:Hollander P is a researcher who participated in the COR-Diabetes Study Group, focusing on the effects of naltrexone/bupropion combination therapy on body weight and glycemic parameters."}{"title": "COR-DIABETES:COR-Diabetes is a study that examines the effects of naltrexone sustained-release/bupropion sustained-release combination therapy on overweight and obese patients with type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "WADDEN TA:Wadden TA is a researcher involved in multiple studies regarding weight loss therapies, including the COR-BMOD trial."}{"title": "NISSEN SE:Nissen SE is a researcher who studied the effect of Naltrexone-Bupropion on major adverse cardiovascular events in overweight and obese patients."}{"title": "LEADER TRIAL:LEADER Trial investigates the cardiovascular outcomes of liraglutide in patients with type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "SCALE DIABETES:SCALE Diabetes is a randomized clinical trial that evaluates the efficacy of liraglutide for weight loss in patients with type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "BLACKMAN A:Blackman A is a researcher who studied the effect of liraglutide in individuals with obesity and obstructive sleep apnea."}{"title": "SCALE SLEEP APNEA:SCALE Sleep Apnea is a randomized clinical trial that examines the effect of liraglutide in individuals with obesity and moderate or severe obstructive sleep apnea."}{"title": "GLUCAGON-LIKE PEPTIDE-1:Glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) is a hormone that plays a crucial role in the regulation of glucose metabolism and appetite. It has garnered significant attention in the context of diabetes treatment and weight management, particularly in relation to the medication liraglutide. Through its functions, GLP-1 contributes to the control of blood sugar levels and helps in managing body weight, making it an important focus in therapeutic strategies for conditions such as diabetes."}{"title": "THIAZOLIDINEDIONE:Thiazolidinedione is a class of medications studied in combination with liraglutide for their effects on type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "SCALE MAINTENANCE:SCALE Maintenance is a randomized study that investigates weight maintenance and additional weight loss with liraglutide after a low-calorie diet."}{"title": "SCALE WEIGHT LOSS:SCALE Weight Loss is a study that evaluates the effectiveness of liraglutide in achieving weight loss in various populations."}{"title": "LEAD-4 MET+TZD:"}{"title": "IRENE BRET\u00d3N:Irene Bret\u00f3n is one of the authors associated with the clinical nutrition and dietetics unit at Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Mara\u00f1\u00f3n in Madrid."}{"title": "CYNTHIA GONZ\u00c1LEZ-ANTIG\u00dcEDAD:Cynthia Gonz\u00e1lez-Antig\u00fcedad is one of the authors associated with the clinical nutrition and dietetics unit at Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Mara\u00f1\u00f3n in Madrid."}{"title": "MARTA MOTILLA:Marta Motilla is one of the authors associated with the clinical nutrition and dietetics unit at Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Mara\u00f1\u00f3n in Madrid."}{"title": "ANA ZUGASTI:Ana Zugasti is one of the authors associated with the clinical nutrition and dietetics unit at Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Mara\u00f1\u00f3n in Madrid."}{"title": "PILAR GARC\u00cdA-PERIS:Pilar Garc\u00eda-Peris is the Head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Mara\u00f1\u00f3n in Madrid. In her role, she oversees nutritional care and research, contributing significantly to the field of clinical nutrition. Additionally, she is recognized as one of the authors associated with the unit, further highlighting her expertise and involvement in advancing nutritional practices and research within the hospital."}{"title": "HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO GREGORIO MARA\u00d1\u00d3N:Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Mara\u00f1\u00f3n is a prominent hospital located in Madrid, known for its specialization in clinical nutrition and dietetics. The hospital plays a significant role in the treatment of eating disorders, providing comprehensive care and support for patients facing these challenges."}{"title": "UNITED KINGDOM:The United Kingdom is a country that has published data on the prevalence of non-communicable diseases, specifically through the BANS registry. Additionally, it is recognized as one of the European countries with high obesity rates, highlighting significant public health concerns within the nation."}{"title": "BULGARIA:Bulgaria is one of the European countries with high obesity rates."}{"title": "HBA1C REDUCTION:HbA1c reduction is a clinical marker that improves with weight loss in obese patients."}{"title": "TESOFENSINE:Tesofensine is a drug studied for its effects on body weight loss and quality of life in obese patients."}{"title": "BELORANIB:Beloranib is a pharmaceutical agent evaluated for weight loss efficacy and safety in obese adults."}{"title": "PYY3-36:PYY3-36 is an enteroendocrine hormone that has been studied for its effects on energy intake and appetite in overweight individuals."}{"title": "GIP-OXYNTOMODULIN HYBRID PEPTIDE:A novel peptide that acts through GIP, glucagon, and GLP-1 receptors, showing weight-reducing properties."}{"title": "RICA:RICA is an organization involved in studies related to obesity prevalence and its implications in health."}{"title": "DI@BET.ES:Di@bet.es is an organization that conducts research on obesity and its related health issues."}{"title": "EEUU:EEUU, or the United States, is a country characterized by a diverse healthcare landscape where coverage and funding for programs such as Medicare and Medicaid vary significantly. This variability extends to laws regarding artificial nutrition, which differ by state, influencing whether such interventions are classified as medical treatments or comfort measures. Additionally, the United States has been the site of significant epidemiological research, particularly concerning intestinal rhythm, as well as studies on the prevalence of gastrointestinal issues like constipation and diarrhea. Furthermore, the country is notable for its healthcare practices, with over 150,000 bariatric surgeries performed annually, reflecting its approach to obesity and related health concerns."}{"title": "DR. MASSON:Dr. Masson is recognized as one of the pioneers of bariatric surgery, proposing the gastric bypass technique in the late 1960s."}{"title": "SOBREPESO:SOBREPESO refers to a condition characterized by an individual having more body weight than is deemed normal or healthy. This condition often serves as a precursor to obesity, which can have various health implications."}{"title": "BANDA G\u00c1STRICA AJUSTABLE:Adjustable gastric banding is a surgical weight-loss procedure that involves placing a band around the upper part of the stomach to limit food intake."}{"title": "MORBIDA:Morbid obesity refers to a condition where an individual has a body mass index (BMI) significantly higher than normal, leading to severe health risks."}{"title": "BANDA G\u00c1STRICA:Banda g\u00e1strica is a surgical technique used for weight loss that creates a small gastric reservoir to limit food intake."}{"title": "GASTRECTOM\u00cdA VERTICAL LAPAROSC\u00d3PICA:Gastrectom\u00eda vertical laparosc\u00f3pica, also known as sleeve gastrectomy, is a minimally invasive surgical technique that removes a large portion of the stomach to aid in weight loss."}{"title": "BANDA G\u00c1STRICA AJUSTABLE LAPAROSC\u00d3PICA:Banda g\u00e1strica ajustable laparosc\u00f3pica is a surgical procedure that involves placing an adjustable band around the stomach to control food intake."}{"title": "SADI:SADI, or single-anastomosis duodeno-ileal, is a surgical method that combines vertical gastrectomy with a duodeno-ileal anastomosis to treat obesity."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICAS QUIR\u00daRGICAS:"}{"title": "CB:CB refers to bariatric surgery, a treatment indicated for patients with severe obesity. This type of surgery can lead to deficiencies in essential nutrients such as folic acid and vitamin B12, making careful monitoring necessary for those who undergo the procedure."}{"title": "COMORBILIDAD:Las comorbilidades son condiciones m\u00e9dicas que pueden acompa\u00f1ar a la obesidad y que pueden mejorar tras la cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica."}{"title": "RIESGO QUIR\u00daRGICO:El riesgo quir\u00fargico es un factor importante a considerar al evaluar a los pacientes para cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N PREOPERATORIA:La evaluaci\u00f3n preoperatoria es un proceso fundamental para seleccionar adecuadamente a los candidatos para la cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica."}{"title": "HTA:HTA, or Hipertensi\u00f3n Arterial, is a medical condition characterized by consistently elevated blood pressure levels. This condition, commonly referred to as hypertension, is often monitored in patients with diabetes due to the associated health risks. HTA can lead to serious health issues and is also recognized as a comorbidity in obese patients, which further increases the risk of complications. Overall, HTA is a significant health concern that requires careful management and monitoring to prevent adverse outcomes."}{"title": "PATOLOG\u00cdA RESPIRATORIA:PATOLOG\u00cdA RESPIRATORIA refers to a range of conditions that impact pulmonary function and can necessitate specific nutritional management. These respiratory pathologies not only affect breathing but can also be comorbidities in patients suffering from obesity."}{"title": "TC:Tomograf\u00eda Computarizada (TC) is a medical imaging technique utilized to visualize internal structures of the body. It plays a crucial role in diagnosing various medical conditions, including those related to anorexia and bulimia. However, the use of TC can be complicated in patients with morbid obesity due to their size, which may pose challenges in obtaining clear images."}{"title": "RM:La resonancia magn\u00e9tica (RM) es una t\u00e9cnica de imagen m\u00e9dica que proporciona im\u00e1genes detalladas de \u00f3rganos y tejidos, siendo especialmente \u00fatil para evaluar cambios neurol\u00f3gicos en pacientes con trastornos alimentarios. Esta prueba diagn\u00f3stica puede ser dif\u00edcil de realizar en pacientes con obesidad m\u00f3rbida, lo que puede complicar su uso en esta poblaci\u00f3n. La RM se utiliza para evaluar la salud de los tejidos blandos y del cerebro en pacientes que padecen trastornos alimentarios, lo que resalta su importancia en el diagn\u00f3stico y seguimiento de estas condiciones."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N PSICOL\u00d3GICA:La evaluaci\u00f3n psicol\u00f3gica es un paso importante en la preparaci\u00f3n de pacientes para cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica, asegurando que est\u00e9n mentalmente preparados para el cambio."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N ANEST\u00c9SICA:"}{"title": "CLINICAL TEAM:The clinical team is composed of healthcare professionals dedicated to supporting and guiding patients throughout the bariatric surgery process, including pre-operative preparation and post-operative care. This team plays a crucial role in monitoring patients after surgery to prevent complications and ensure that they receive appropriate follow-up care. Their comprehensive approach aims to facilitate a successful recovery and promote the overall well-being of patients undergoing bariatric procedures."}{"title": "PRIMARY CARE TEAMS:Primary care teams collaborate closely with the clinical team to ensure comprehensive care for the patient post-surgery."}{"title": "HYDRATION:Hydration is a vital process that involves maintaining adequate fluid intake, which plays a significant role in various health contexts. It is particularly critical in preventing kidney stones, as proper hydration helps to dilute urine and reduce the crystallization of minerals that can lead to stone formation. Additionally, hydration is essential for patients who have undergone bariatric surgery, as it helps prevent complications associated with insufficient fluid intake. Overall, maintaining proper hydration is crucial for overall health and well-being."}{"title": "ALCOHOL INTAKE:Alcohol intake is discouraged post-bariatric surgery due to its potential effects on nutrient absorption and the risk of addiction."}{"title": "COMPLICATIONS:Complications refer to potential health issues that may arise following bariatric surgery, necessitating careful monitoring and management."}{"title": "OMEPRAZOLE:Omeprazole is a medication recommended for use after bariatric surgery to reduce gastroesophageal reflux."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL COMPLICATIONS:Nutritional complications are frequent after bariatric surgery, including protein malnutrition and micronutrient deficiencies."}{"title": "PRIMARY CARE:Primary care is involved in the protocolized coordination for the follow-up of patients after bariatric surgery."}{"title": "GASTRIC BYPASS:Gastric bypass is a surgical procedure for weight loss that alters the digestive system and can result in complications such as nutritional deficiencies."}{"title": "TEP:TEP refers to thromboembolic events, which are potential complications that can occur during or after bariatric surgery."}{"title": "PROTEIN MALNUTRITION:Protein malnutrition is a serious complication that can occur following bariatric surgery, especially after procedures such as biliopancreatic diversion. This condition is characterized by a range of symptoms, including edema, asthenia (weakness), hair loss, and an increased susceptibility to infections. It highlights the importance of monitoring nutritional status in patients who have undergone such surgical interventions to prevent and address potential deficiencies."}{"title": "MICRONUTRIENT DEFICIENCIES:Micronutrient deficiencies are common complications following bariatric surgery, necessitating careful monitoring and supplementation."}{"title": "BILIARY-PANCREATIC DIVERSION:"}{"title": "DERIVACI\u00d3N BILI PANCRE\u00c1TICA:A surgical procedure that can lead to serious complications such as protein malnutrition and micronutrient deficiencies, particularly in the first year post-surgery."}{"title": "MICRONUTRIENT DEFICIENCY:Common in patients undergoing bariatric surgery, it can be prevented or treated early with proper follow-up and supplementation."}{"title": "MAGNESIUM:Magnesium is a vital micronutrient and mineral that plays a critical role in numerous biological functions and processes within the body. It is essential for bone health and is involved in over 300 biochemical reactions, including those that regulate heart health. While magnesium deficiency is rare, it can occur in specific populations, such as patients experiencing significant diarrhea or those with liver disease, particularly in cases related to alcohol consumption. Dietary reference intake guidelines for magnesium are specified for different age groups, highlighting its importance across the lifespan. Additionally, magnesium contributes to the prevention of kidney stones by inhibiting crystallization, further underscoring its significance in maintaining overall health."}{"title": "VITAMINAS A, E Y K:Vitamins A, E, and K are fat-soluble vitamins that can be deficient after malabsorptive techniques, necessitating specific supplementation."}{"title": "BILIOPANCRE\u00c1TICA:Biliopancreatic diversion is a type of surgery that can lead to deficiencies in zinc, copper, and other micronutrients."}{"title": "GLUCOSE MONITORING:Glucose monitoring is a process used to track blood sugar levels, particularly in patients who have undergone bariatric surgery."}{"title": "DENSITY MINERAL BONE:Bone mineral density refers to the amount of mineral matter per square centimeter of bones, which can decrease after bariatric surgery."}{"title": "MULTIVITAMIN:Multivitamins are dietary supplements that may be recommended for patients post-bariatric surgery to prevent nutrient deficiencies."}{"title": "ACARBOSE:Acarbose is a medication that can be used to manage postprandial hyperglycemia in patients who have undergone bariatric surgery."}{"title": "BAND GASTRIC:Band gastric is a type of bariatric surgery that involves placing a band around the stomach to restrict food intake."}{"title": "VERTICAL GASTRECTOMY:Vertical gastrectomy is a surgical procedure for weight loss that involves removing a portion of the stomach."}{"title": "BPG:BPG refers to a type of bariatric surgery that may require specific nutritional supplementation post-operation."}{"title": "SYNDROME DE DUMPING:"}{"title": "PRECLAMPSIA:La preeclampsia es una complicaci\u00f3n del embarazo que se presenta con hipertensi\u00f3n y puede ser m\u00e1s com\u00fan en mujeres obesas."}{"title": "MACROSOM\u00cdA:La macrosom\u00eda se refiere a un beb\u00e9 que es significativamente m\u00e1s grande que el promedio, y puede ser un riesgo en embarazos de mujeres obesas."}{"title": "SEGUIMIENTO CL\u00cdNICO:El seguimiento cl\u00ednico es esencial para los pacientes que han tenido cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica para asegurar la p\u00e9rdida de peso y minimizar complicaciones."}{"title": "SIMONELLI:Simonelli A. is an author who contributed to the research on biliopancreatic diversion published in the World Journal of Surgery in 1998."}{"title": "LARRAD-JIM\u00c9NEZ:Larrad-Jim\u00e9nez A. is an author who studied the results of biliopancreatic diversion and published findings in Obesity Surgery in 2007."}{"title": "BALTASAR:Baltasar A. is an author who discussed surgical treatment for morbid obesity in a publication in Cirug\u00eda Espa\u00f1ola in May 2004."}{"title": "S\u00c1NCHEZ-PERNAUTE:S\u00e1nchez-Pernaute A. is an author who researched single anastomosis duodeno-ileal bypass with sleeve gastrectomy and published results in Obesity Surgery in 2010."}{"title": "CARDOSO:Cardoso L. is an author who conducted a systematic review on mortality after bariatric surgery, published in Diabetes Obesity and Metabolism in 2017."}{"title": "KASKA:Kaska L. is an author who studied glucose metabolism improvements following bariatric surgery, published in World Journal of Gastroenterology in 2016."}{"title": "RUBIO:Rubio M.A. is an author of a consensus document on bariatric surgery published in Revista Espa\u00f1ola de Obesidad in 2004."}{"title": "MORALES:Morales MJ is an author who discussed surgical treatment for obesity and its follow-up in Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n in 2004."}{"title": "ESQUIDE:Esquide J.L. is an author who wrote about anesthesia in bariatric surgery published in Cirug\u00eda Espa\u00f1ola in 2004."}{"title": "FRIS:Fris R.J. is an author who researched the effects of a preoperative low energy diet on liver size, published in Obesity Surgery in 2004."}{"title": "COLLES:Colles S.L. is an author who studied preoperative weight loss effects on liver and abdominal fat, published in the American Journal of Clinical Nutrition in 2006."}{"title": "MECHANICK:Mechanick J.I. is an author of clinical practice guidelines for bariatric surgery patients, published in Obesity (Silver Spring) in 2013."}{"title": "ELLIOTT:Elliott J.A. is an author who conducted a systematic review on fast-track laparoscopic bariatric surgery, published in Updates in Surgery in 2013."}{"title": "ALVAREZ:Alvarez J. is an author who provided nutritional recommendations for obesity in a manual published by Novartis Health Consumer S.A. in 2001."}{"title": "MARCASON:Marcason W. is an author who discussed dietary guidelines following bariatric surgery in the Journal of the American Dietetic Association in 2004."}{"title": "LEEVY:Leevy C.M. is an author who wrote about nutritional aspects of alcoholic liver disease in Clinical Liver Disease in 2005."}{"title": "SVENSSON:Svensson P.A. is an author who studied alcohol consumption and problems after bariatric surgery, published in Obesity (Silver Spring) in 2013."}{"title": "BILIOPANCREATIC DIVERSION:Biliopancreatic diversion is a surgical procedure primarily aimed at treating obesity. It is classified as a type of weight-loss surgery that entails the removal of a portion of the stomach, along with the rerouting of the intestines. This procedure has been the subject of various studies, highlighting its significance in the management of obesity."}{"title": "DE CUADROS BORRAJO:de Cuadros Borrajo P. is an author who co-authored a study on biliopancreatic diversion published in Obesity Surgery in 2007."}{"title": "LESMES:Lesmes I.B. is an author who contributed to the research on biliopancreatic diversion published in Obesity Surgery in 2007."}{"title": "ESTEBAN:Esteban B.M. is an author who co-authored a study on biliopancreatic diversion published in Obesity Surgery in 2007."}{"title": "MART\u00cdN-ANTONA:Mart\u00edn-Antona E. is an author who contributed to the study of biliopancreatic diversion published in Obesity Surgery in 2007."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA-BOTELLA:Garc\u00eda-Botella A. is an author who co-authored a study on biliopancreatic diversion published in Obesity Surgery in 2007."}{"title": "GARCIA-ALMENTA:Garcia-Almenta E.M. is an author who contributed to the study of biliopancreatic diversion published in Obesity Surgery in 2007."}{"title": "TORRES:Torres A. is an author who co-authored a study on biliopancreatic diversion published in Obesity Surgery in 2007."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA ESPA\u00d1OLA:Cirug\u00eda Espa\u00f1ola is a medical journal that published various studies related to bariatric surgery."}{"title": "WORLD JOURNAL OF SURGERY:The World Journal of Surgery is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research related to surgical techniques and outcomes on a global scale. It features studies on various surgical procedures, including biliopancreatic diversion, among other topics. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating significant findings in the field of surgery, contributing to the advancement of surgical practices and knowledge worldwide."}{"title": "D\u00cdAZ-GUERRA:"}{"title": "LEEVY CM:Leevy CM is a researcher who has contributed to the study of nutritional aspects of alcoholic liver disease."}{"title": "MOROIANU SA:Moroianu SA is a researcher involved in the study of nutritional aspects of alcoholic liver disease."}{"title": "SWEDISH OBESE SUBJECTS STUDY:The Swedish Obese Subjects Study is a research study examining the effects of bariatric surgery on obesity and related health issues."}{"title": "CHIAPPETTA S:Chiappetta S is a researcher who has studied refeeding syndrome following obesity surgery."}{"title": "STEIN J:Stein J is a researcher who has studied refeeding syndrome following obesity surgery."}{"title": "J\u00c1UREGUI-LOBERA I:J\u00e1uregui-Lobera I is a researcher focused on iron deficiency and bariatric surgery."}{"title": "JERIC\u00d3 C:Jeric\u00f3 C is a researcher involved in the diagnosis and treatment of iron deficiency related to bariatric surgery."}{"title": "BRET\u00d3N I:Bret\u00f3n I is a researcher involved in the diagnosis and treatment of iron deficiency related to bariatric surgery."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA RUIZ DE GORDEJUELA A:Garc\u00eda Ruiz de Gordejuela A is a researcher involved in the diagnosis and treatment of iron deficiency related to bariatric surgery."}{"title": "DE OLIVEIRA AC:De Oliveira AC is a researcher involved in the diagnosis and treatment of iron deficiency related to bariatric surgery."}{"title": "RUBIO M\u00c1:Rubio M\u00c1 is a researcher involved in the diagnosis and treatment of iron deficiency related to bariatric surgery."}{"title": "TINAHONES FJ:Tinahones FJ is a researcher involved in the diagnosis and treatment of iron deficiency related to bariatric surgery."}{"title": "VIDAL J:Vidal J is a researcher involved in the diagnosis and treatment of iron deficiency related to bariatric surgery."}{"title": "VILARRASA N:Vilarrasa N is a researcher involved in the diagnosis and treatment of iron deficiency related to bariatric surgery."}{"title": "SCHAFFER AL:Schafer AL is a researcher studying intestinal calcium absorption after gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "WEAVER CM:Weaver CM is a researcher focused on the study of intestinal calcium absorption following gastric bypass surgery. In addition to this research, Weaver CM is also an author who discusses the calcium requirements of physically active individuals. This dual role highlights Weaver CM's expertise in both the physiological aspects of calcium absorption and the nutritional needs of those engaged in physical activity."}{"title": "WHEELER AL:Wheeler AL is a researcher studying intestinal calcium absorption after gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "CHANG H:Chang H is a researcher studying intestinal calcium absorption after gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "SZEFK GV:Szefk GV is a researcher studying intestinal calcium absorption after gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "STEWART L:Stewart L is a researcher studying intestinal calcium absorption after gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "ROGERS SJ:Rogers SJ is a researcher studying intestinal calcium absorption after gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "CARTER JT:Carter JT is a researcher studying intestinal calcium absorption after gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "POSSELT AM:Posselt AM is a researcher studying intestinal calcium absorption after gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "SHOBACK DM:Shoback DM is a researcher studying intestinal calcium absorption after gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "SELLMEYER DE:Sellmeyer DE is a researcher studying intestinal calcium absorption after gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "DE LUIS DA:De Luis DA is a prominent researcher engaged in various clinical trials that explore the intersection of nutrition and cancer, with a particular emphasis on enteral nutrition and its impact on patients. His work extends to studying the serum levels of zinc and copper in morbidly obese patients following biliopancreatic diversion, highlighting his focus on nutritional deficiencies in this population. Additionally, De Luis DA has made significant contributions to the field of home enteral nutrition in Spain, advocating for its importance in patient care. He is also an author who has addressed evidence-based nutrition practices in the context of acute pancreatitis and chronic liver disease, further underscoring his commitment to advancing nutritional science in clinical settings."}{"title": "PACHECO D:Pacheco D is a researcher studying zinc and copper serum levels in morbidly obese patients after biliopancreatic diversion."}{"title": "IZAOLA O:Izaola O is a researcher studying zinc and copper serum levels in morbidly obese patients after biliopancreatic diversion."}{"title": "GLETSU-MILLER N:Gletsu-Miller N is a researcher studying copper deficiency following gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "BRODERIUS M:Broderius M is a researcher studying copper deficiency following gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "FREDIANI JK:Frediani JK is a researcher studying copper deficiency following gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "ZHAO VM:Zhao VM is a researcher studying copper deficiency following gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "GRIFFITH DP:Griffith DP is a researcher studying copper deficiency following gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "DAVIS SS JR:Davis SS Jr is a researcher studying copper deficiency following gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "SWEENEY JF:Sweeney JF is a researcher studying copper deficiency following gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "LIN E:Lin E is a researcher studying copper deficiency following gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "PROHASKA JR:Prohaska JR is a researcher studying copper deficiency following gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "ZIEGLER TR:Ziegler TR is a prominent researcher and author known for his extensive studies in the field of nutrition and its impact on various medical conditions. He has specifically focused on the efficacy and safety of glutamine-supplemented parenteral nutrition in surgical ICU patients, highlighting the importance of this amino acid in critical care settings. Additionally, Ziegler has investigated the clinical efficacy of glutamine in nutrition following bone marrow transplantation, further emphasizing its role in recovery and immune function. His research also extends to the study of copper deficiency that can occur after gastric bypass surgery, showcasing his interest in the nutritional challenges faced by patients undergoing significant surgical procedures. Furthermore, Ziegler has explored how glutamine regulates immune cell function, contributing to a deeper understanding of its potential benefits in various therapeutic contexts. Overall, Ziegler TR's work significantly advances the knowledge of nutritional interventions in critical and post-surgical care."}{"title": "BALSA JA:Balsa JA is a researcher studying nutritional deficiency of selenium after bariatric surgery."}{"title": "BOTELLA-CARRETERO JI:Botella-Carretero JI is a researcher focused on the nutritional deficiency of selenium following bariatric surgery. In addition to this area of study, Botella-Carretero JI has also authored research on nutrition in the context of acute pancreatitis. This dual focus highlights their expertise in the field of nutrition, particularly in relation to surgical interventions and acute medical conditions."}{"title": "G\u00d3MEZ-MART\u00cdN JM:G\u00f3mez-Mart\u00edn JM is a researcher studying nutritional deficiency of selenium after bariatric surgery."}{"title": "MAHAWAR KK:Mahawar KK is a researcher studying zinc deficiency after gastric bypass for morbid obesity."}{"title": "BHASKER AG:Bhasker AG is a researcher studying zinc deficiency after gastric bypass for morbid obesity."}{"title": "BINDAL V:Bindal V is a researcher studying zinc deficiency after gastric bypass for morbid obesity."}{"title": "GRAHAM Y:Graham Y is a researcher studying zinc deficiency after gastric bypass for morbid obesity."}{"title": "DUDEJA U:Dudeja U is a researcher studying zinc deficiency after gastric bypass for morbid obesity."}{"title": "LAKDAWALA M:Lakdawala M is a researcher studying zinc deficiency after gastric bypass for morbid obesity."}{"title": "SMALL PK:Small PK is a researcher studying zinc deficiency after gastric bypass for morbid obesity."}{"title": "WENG TC:Weng TC is a researcher studying anemia and related nutrient deficiencies after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "CHANG CH:Chang CH is a researcher studying anemia and related nutrient deficiencies after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "DONG YH:Dong YH is a researcher studying anemia and related nutrient deficiencies after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "CHANG YC:Chang YC is a researcher studying anemia and related nutrient deficiencies after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "CHUANG LM:Chuang LM is a researcher studying anemia and related nutrient deficiencies after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "KIM HJ:Kim HJ is a researcher studying anemia and related nutrient deficiencies after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "LO MENZO E:Lo Menzo E(\"entity\""}{"title": "ROUX-EN-Y GASTRIC BYPASS:Roux-en-Y gastric bypass is a type of weight-loss surgery that involves creating a small pouch from the stomach and connecting it directly to the small intestine."}{"title": "SLEEVE GASTRECTOMY:Sleeve gastrectomy is a surgical procedure for weight loss that involves removing a large portion of the stomach, leaving a tube-like structure."}{"title": "VITAMIN B12 DEFICIENCY:Vitamin B12 deficiency is a common issue following bariatric surgery, leading to various health complications."}{"title": "MICRONUTRIENT SUPPLEMENTATION:Micronutrient supplementation refers to the intake of vitamins and minerals to prevent deficiencies, particularly after bariatric surgery."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL DEFICIENCY:Nutritional deficiency occurs when the body does not receive an adequate supply of essential nutrients, leading to various health issues. This condition is particularly concerning in vulnerable populations, such as infants, who may suffer significant health consequences due to insufficient nutrient intake. Additionally, nutritional deficiency can arise after bariatric surgery, where changes in the digestive system may hinder the absorption of vital nutrients. Furthermore, it is important to note that a lack of essential nutrients can exacerbate the symptoms and progression of conditions such as ELA (Eosinophilic Esophagitis), highlighting the critical role that proper nutrition plays in overall health and disease management."}{"title": "CALCIUM AND VITAMIN D DEPLETION:Calcium and vitamin D depletion can occur after certain types of bariatric surgery, affecting bone health."}{"title": "GUIDELINES ON VITAMIN D REPLACEMENT:Guidelines on vitamin D replacement provide recommendations for managing vitamin D levels in patients undergoing bariatric surgery."}{"title": "M.\u00aa CRISTINA CUERDA COMP\u00c9S:Adjunct physician at the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Mara\u00f1\u00f3n, specializing in nutritional support for eating disorders."}{"title": "MARTA MOTILLA DE LA C\u00c1MARA:Adjunct physician at the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Mara\u00f1\u00f3n, focusing on nutritional therapy."}{"title": "LOREDANA ARHIP:Dietitian-Nutritionist at the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Mara\u00f1\u00f3n, providing dietary support for patients."}{"title": "TRASTORNO POR ATRAC\u00d3N:TRASTORNO POR ATRAC\u00d3N is an eating disorder that is characterized by recurrent episodes of binge eating, where individuals consume large quantities of food in a short period of time. Unlike other eating disorders, such as bulimia nervosa, individuals with trastorno por atrac\u00f3n do not engage in subsequent purging behaviors or inappropriate compensatory actions. This disorder often leads to significant distress for those affected. In summary, trastorno por atrac\u00f3n is defined by its compulsive eating episodes without the presence of purging, distinguishing it from other eating disorders."}{"title": "MUJERES ADOLESCENTES:Grupo demogr\u00e1fico que presenta una prevalencia significativa de trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, especialmente en pa\u00edses occidentales."}{"title": "MODELOS:Grupo profesional que parece estar m\u00e1s afectado por trastornos de la conducta alimentaria debido a presiones sociales sobre la imagen corporal."}{"title": "ATLETAS:Grupo profesional que tambi\u00e9n muestra una mayor incidencia de trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, posiblemente debido a la presi\u00f3n para mantener un peso espec\u00edfico."}{"title": "GIMNASTAS:Grupo profesional que se encuentra en riesgo elevado de desarrollar trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, similar a modelos y atletas."}{"title": "BAJA AUTOESTIMA:La baja autoestima es un factor de riesgo significativo para el desarrollo de trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, afectando a muchos pacientes."}{"title": "OBESIDAD INFANTIL:La obesidad infantil es un antecedente que puede aumentar el riesgo de desarrollar trastornos de la conducta alimentaria en la adolescencia."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES NEUROQU\u00cdMICAS:Las alteraciones neuroqu\u00edmicas, como la disregulaci\u00f3n de la serotonina, son factores biol\u00f3gicos que pueden contribuir a los trastornos de la conducta alimentaria."}{"title": "FACTORES DE MAL PRON\u00d3STICO:Los factores de mal pron\u00f3stico en los trastornos de la conducta alimentaria incluyen v\u00f3mitos, conductas purgativas y p\u00e9rdida de peso importante."}{"title": "FACTORES DE BUEN PRON\u00d3STICO:Los factores de buen pron\u00f3stico incluyen el inicio en adolescentes j\u00f3venes y una duraci\u00f3n corta de la enfermedad."}{"title": "ASOCIACI\u00d3N AMERICANA DE PSIQUIATR\u00cdA:The American Psychiatric Association is a professional organization that publishes diagnostic criteria for mental disorders, including eating disorders."}{"title": "ANSIEDAD:Anxiety is another psychiatric condition frequently observed in patients with eating disorders, contributing to their overall psychological profile."}{"title": "TRAUMAS PSICOL\u00d3GICOS:Psychological traumas can influence the development of eating disorders, affecting patients' mental health and coping mechanisms."}{"title": "DIN\u00c1MICA FAMILIAR:Family dynamics can significantly impact the psychological well-being of patients with eating disorders, often contributing to their condition."}{"title": "PSICOTERAPIA:PSICOTERAPIA es un tratamiento que implica la interacci\u00f3n entre un paciente y un terapeuta, utilizado para abordar trastornos psicol\u00f3gicos, incluyendo los trastornos de la conducta alimentaria. Este enfoque terap\u00e9utico es fundamental en el tratamiento de los trastornos alimentarios, ya que se centra en tratar los problemas psicol\u00f3gicos subyacentes y fomentar la recuperaci\u00f3n del paciente."}{"title": "VALORACI\u00d3N INICIAL:Initial assessment for patients with eating disorders includes various tests such as hemogram, glucose levels, and renal function tests."}{"title": "PRUEBAS A CONSIDERAR:Subsequent tests for evaluating patients with eating disorders may include serum iron, hormonal levels, and gastrointestinal studies."}{"title": "MANIFESTACIONES CL\u00cdNICAS:Clinical manifestations of eating disorders are multisystemic due to malnutrition, affecting almost all parts of the body and potentially causing irreversible damage."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES CARDIOVASCULARES:Cardiovascular alterations in patients with anorexia nerviosa include bradycardia, hypotension, and various electrocardiographic abnormalities."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES DIGESTIVAS:ALTERACIONES DIGESTIVAS refer to a range of digestive issues commonly associated with anorexia nerviosa. These alterations include decreased gastrointestinal motility and delayed gastric emptying, which can significantly impact the digestive process. Additionally, these digestive disorders can affect nutrient absorption, potentially necessitating the use of enteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutrient intake."}{"title": "GASTROPARESIA:Gastroparesis is a medical condition that affects the stomach muscles, preventing proper stomach emptying. It is often observed in diabetic patients and can lead to significant weight loss, particularly in cases such as anorexia nervosa. The condition is characterized by delayed gastric emptying, which can result in increased gastric residue, especially in patients receiving enteral nutrition. Improvement in gastroparesis symptoms is typically achieved through nutritional rehabilitation and dietary adjustments."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNAS VISCERALES:Visceral proteins are evaluated in the initial assessment to assess nutritional status and liver function in patients with eating disorders."}{"title": "ESTUDIO LIP\u00cdDICO:Lipid studies are conducted to evaluate the fat levels in the blood, which can be affected by eating disorders."}{"title": "FUNCIONES RENAL:Renal function tests are conducted to evaluate kidney health, which can be impacted by malnutrition in eating disorder patients."}{"title": "FUNCIONES HEP\u00c1TICAS:Liver function tests are performed to assess the health of the liver, which can be affected by eating disorders."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LISIS ELEMENTAL DE ORINA:Urine elemental analysis is performed to assess metabolic and nutritional status in patients with eating disorders."}{"title": "ELECTROCARDIOGRAMA:Electrocardiogram is a test used to monitor heart activity, which can be affected by eating disorders, particularly anorexia nerviosa."}{"title": "HIERRO S\u00c9RICO:Serum iron levels are tested to assess iron deficiency, which can occur in patients with eating disorders."}{"title": "NIVELES DE VITAMINAS:Vitamin levels are assessed to monitor nutritional deficiencies that can arise in patients with eating disorders."}{"title": "AMILASA S\u00c9RICA:Serum amylase levels are tested to evaluate pancreatic function, which can be affected by eating disorders."}{"title": "ESTUDIOS DEL TRACTO GASTROINTESTINAL:Gastrointestinal studies are conducted to assess digestive health and complications in patients with eating disorders."}{"title": "TC CRANEAL:Cranial CT scan is used to assess brain health and detect any complications related to eating disorders."}{"title": "ECOCARDIOGRAMA:Echocardiogram is used to assess heart structure and function, which can be affected by eating disorders.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTION:An institution that may provide psychological and nutritional education to patients recovering from eating disorders."}{"title": "ALCALOSIS METAB\u00d3LICA HIPOCLOREMICA:Alcalosis metab\u00f3lica hipoclor\u00e9mica is a metabolic disorder that can occur in patients with Bulimia Nervosa as a result of vomiting."}{"title": "AMENORREA:Amenorrhea is defined as the absence of menstruation and can manifest in two forms: primary and secondary. This condition is often observed in individuals with Anorexia Nervosa, where it is primarily linked to hormonal imbalances. In patients suffering from Anorexia Nervosa, the disruption of normal hormonal function can lead to the cessation of menstrual cycles, highlighting the significant impact of this eating disorder on reproductive health."}{"title": "EDUCACI\u00d3N PSICOL\u00d3GICA:Psicological education is crucial for patients recovering from eating disorders, helping them understand their conditions and develop coping strategies."}{"title": "REVISI\u00d3N DENTAL:Dental check-ups are recommended for patients with Bulimia Nervosa to monitor and address dental health issues caused by vomiting."}{"title": "17-BETA ESTRADIOL:17-Beta Estradiol is a form of estrogen used in hormone replacement therapy, which has been studied for its effects on bone mass in adolescents with Anorexia Nervosa."}{"title": "DHEAS:Dehydroepiandrosterone sulfate (DHEAS) is a hormone that has shown controversial results when administered alongside oral contraceptives in patients with Anorexia Nervosa."}{"title": "TERIPARATIDE:Teriparatide is a medication that has demonstrated significant improvement in bone mass and increased bone density in adult women suffering from Anorexia Nervosa after a short treatment period. This treatment is particularly beneficial for addressing the bone health challenges faced by women with this eating disorder."}{"title": "BONE DENSITOMETRY:Bone densitometry is a diagnostic procedure recommended for patients with Anorexia Nervosa who have experienced amenorrhea for more than six months to assess bone density."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL REHABILITATION:Nutritional rehabilitation involves the process of restoring nutritional health in individuals suffering from eating disorders, particularly anorexia nervosa. This approach aims to address the deficiencies and imbalances in nutrition that can arise from such disorders, facilitating recovery and promoting overall well-being."}{"title": "GHRELIN:Ghrelin is a hormone that plays a significant role in regulating appetite and influencing various hormonal releases, particularly in patients with anorexia nervosa. Research has shown that ghrelin levels are elevated in individuals suffering from anorexia nervosa, indicating a state of negative energy balance. This elevation suggests that ghrelin may be involved in the physiological responses associated with this eating disorder, highlighting its importance in understanding appetite regulation and energy homeostasis in affected patients."}{"title": "ESTROGENS:Estrogens are hormones whose production decreases in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa due to loss of weight and fat mass."}{"title": "MENSTRUATION:Menstruation recovery is an important indicator of healing in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa."}{"title": "RT3:Reverse T3 (rT3) is a thyroid hormone that may be elevated in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa, indicating metabolic adaptation to malnutrition."}{"title": "MOTIVACI\u00d3N:Motivation is a key factor in the treatment of patients with eating disorders, influencing their willingness to normalize eating habits and collaborate in treatment."}{"title": "CREATININE EXCRETION:Creatinine excretion refers to the measurement of creatinine levels in urine collected over a 24-hour period. This metric is utilized to assess muscle mass in individuals, providing valuable insights into their overall health. Specifically, in patients with chronic liver disease, 24-hour urine samples of creatinine excretion serve as an important method for evaluating muscle mass, which can be affected by the condition. Thus, creatinine excretion is a significant indicator in both general health assessments and in the context of chronic liver disease."}{"title": "24-HOUR URINE TEST:The 24-hour urine test measures various substances, including creatinine, to evaluate muscle mass and nutritional status."}{"title": "AN:AN, which stands for Anorexia Nervosa, is a type of eating disorder that significantly impacts dietary habits and caloric intake."}{"title": "MEN\u00da:MEN\u00da refers to a planned list of foods designed to assist patients with eating disorders in establishing healthy eating habits. Additionally, it serves as a structured meal plan that adheres to dietary restrictions for patients undergoing dialysis, specifically focusing on low potassium and phosphorus intake. This dual purpose highlights the importance of tailored nutritional guidance for individuals with specific health needs."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN GRASAS SALUDABLES:Alimentos ricos en grasas saludables, such as fatty fish and olive oil, are recommended for patients with bulimia nervosa. These foods provide essential nutrients and can support overall health while addressing the specific dietary needs of individuals dealing with this eating disorder."}{"title": "ATRACONES:Binge eating episodes are a significant concern for patients with bulimia nervosa, requiring careful dietary planning."}{"title": "LAXANTES:Laxantes are substances that play a significant role in altering bowel movements and are commonly used to treat constipation. They function through various mechanisms to facilitate bowel movements, making them an essential option for individuals experiencing this condition. However, laxantes can also impact the results of breath tests for carbohydrate malabsorption, which is an important consideration in clinical settings. Additionally, laxatives are often misused by patients with bulimia nervosa, leading to complications that can adversely affect their dietary needs. Overall, while laxantes serve a critical purpose in managing constipation, their misuse and potential effects on diagnostic tests highlight the need for careful monitoring and responsible use."}{"title": "COMIDAS FRECUENTES:Frequent small meals are suggested to help patients with bulimia nervosa manage their eating patterns.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "VACIAMIENTO G\u00c1STRICO R\u00c1PIDO:Condici\u00f3n que puede requerir un enfoque espec\u00edfico en la ingesta de alimentos s\u00f3lidos y la eliminaci\u00f3n de az\u00facares simples."}{"title": "RECUPERACI\u00d3N PONDERAL:Proceso de restaurar el peso corporal saludable en pacientes con trastornos de la conducta alimentaria."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES COGNITIVAS Y CONDUCTUALES:Cambios en el comportamiento y la percepci\u00f3n que pueden ocurrir en pacientes desnutridos y que mejoran con la recuperaci\u00f3n del peso."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO AMBULATORIO:Enfoque de tratamiento que permite a los pacientes recibir atenci\u00f3n sin ser hospitalizados."}{"title": "MOTIVOS DE INGRESO:Razones que pueden llevar a un paciente a ser hospitalizado, ya sean m\u00e9dicas o psiqui\u00e1tricas."}{"title": "HOSPITALES DE D\u00cdA:Centros que ofrecen tratamiento a pacientes durante el d\u00eda, permitiendo que regresen a casa por la noche."}{"title": "AUSTRALIA Y NUEVA ZELANDA:Australia y Nueva Zelanda son pa\u00edses que tienen gu\u00edas para la realimentaci\u00f3n de pacientes desnutridos con anorexia nerviosa, recomendando un aporte cal\u00f3rico de 15-20 kcal/kg."}{"title": "MARSIPAN:MARSIPAN, Management of Really Sick Patients with Anorexia Nervosa, es una gu\u00eda del Reino Unido para el manejo de pacientes con anorexia nerviosa."}{"title": "PACIENTES CON AN:Los pacientes con anorexia nerviosa (AN) son aquellos que sufren de desnutrici\u00f3n y requieren un manejo cuidadoso durante la realimentaci\u00f3n para evitar complicaciones."}{"title": "JUNIOR MARSIPAN:Junior MARSIPAN es una gu\u00eda del Reino Unido destinada a pacientes menores de 18 a\u00f1os con anorexia nerviosa, que tambi\u00e9n incluye recomendaciones sobre la realimentaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "ROYAL COLLEGE OF PSYCHIATRISTS:"}{"title": "GU\u00cdAS NICE:Las gu\u00edas NICE son directrices que proporcionan recomendaciones sobre la atenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica y el tratamiento, incluyendo la identificaci\u00f3n de pacientes con alto riesgo de s\u00edndrome de realimentaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "K:El potasio (K) es un electrolito que se monitorea en pacientes durante la realimentaci\u00f3n para prevenir complicaciones como el s\u00edndrome de realimentaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "MG:El magnesio (Mg) es otro electrolito que se vigila en pacientes durante la realimentaci\u00f3n para prevenir complicaciones asociadas a la desnutrici\u00f3n."}{"title": "SOCIETY OF MEDICINE OF ADOLESCENTS:The Society of Medicine of Adolescents is an organization that provides recommendations for the treatment of adolescents, particularly in relation to nutrition and eating disorders."}{"title": "BULIMIA NERVOSA:Bulimia Nervosa is an eating disorder marked by binge eating followed by purging, which can lead to serious health complications."}{"title": "FAIRBURN CG:Fairburn CG is a researcher known for contributions to the understanding and treatment of eating disorders, particularly Bulimia Nervosa."}{"title": "HARRISON PJ:Harrison PJ is a researcher who has co-authored studies on eating disorders, contributing to the understanding of their psychological aspects."}{"title": "SEINHAUSEN HC:Seinhausen HC is a researcher who has studied the outcomes of Anorexia Nervosa, particularly in the 20th century."}{"title": "MEHLER PS:Mehler PS is a physician and researcher recognized for his contributions to the understanding and treatment of Anorexia Nervosa and Bulimia Nervosa. He has published research focusing on the medical complications associated with these eating disorders, as well as their treatment and management. His work also encompasses related nutritional issues, highlighting his expertise in addressing the complexities of these conditions."}{"title": "ZIPFEL S:Zipfel S is a researcher who has studied the effects of eating disorders on bone health, particularly osteoporosis."}{"title": "REFEEDING SYNDROME:Refeeding syndrome is a potentially fatal condition that can arise when feeding is resumed in individuals who are malnourished. This syndrome is particularly relevant in the treatment of eating disorders, such as anorexia nervosa, and is also a significant concern for malnourished patients receiving parenteral nutrition. The condition underscores the risks associated with reintroducing nutrition to individuals who have been in a state of starvation or severe malnutrition, highlighting the need for careful management and monitoring during the refeeding process."}{"title": "MILLER KK:Miller KK is a researcher who has contributed to studies on the treatment of anorexia nervosa and its effects on bone density."}{"title": "GRINSPOON S:Grinspoon S is a researcher involved in the study of endocrine aspects and treatments related to anorexia nervosa."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF EATING DISORDERS:The Journal of Eating Disorders is a publication that focuses on research and treatment of eating disorders, including anorexia nervosa."}{"title": "ALENDRONATE:Alendronate is a medication used to treat osteopenia and osteoporosis, which has been studied in the context of anorexia nervosa."}{"title": "RIBOFLAVIN:Riboflavin is a vitamin that has been studied in relation to nutritional status in adolescent girls with anorexia nervosa."}{"title": "GENTILE MG:Gentile MG is a researcher who has contributed to studies on nutritional rehabilitation and treatment protocols for anorexia nervosa."}{"title": "O'CONNOR G:O'Connor G is a researcher involved in studies related to refeeding protocols and nutritional management in adolescents with anorexia nervosa."}{"title": "GARBER AK:Garber AK is a researcher who has examined weight gain and nutritional protocols in hospitalized adolescents with anorexia nervosa."}{"title": "STANGA Z:Stanga Z is a researcher who has published work on the refeeding syndrome and guidelines for its prevention and treatment."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF AMERICAN DIETETIC ASSOCIATION:The Journal of the American Dietetic Association publishes research and guidelines on nutrition and dietetics, including treatment for eating disorders."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF NUTRITION AND METABOLISM:The Journal of Nutrition and Metabolism publishes research on nutritional interventions and their effects on health, including studies on anorexia nervosa."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF ADOLESCENT HEALTH:The Journal of Adolescent Health publishes research on health issues affecting adolescents, including studies on eating disorders and nutritional interventions."}{"title": "NUTRITION CLINICAL PRACTICE:Nutrition Clinical Practice is a journal dedicated to offering insights into clinical nutrition practices and disseminating research findings. It serves as a valuable resource for professionals in the field by providing guidelines and research related to clinical nutrition, including the treatment of eating disorders. Through its publications, the journal aims to enhance the understanding and application of clinical nutrition in various healthcare settings."}{"title": "CLINICAL PATHOLOGY:"}{"title": "SOCIETY FOR ADOLESCENT HEALTH AND MEDICINE:The Society for Adolescent Health and Medicine is an organization focused on the health and medical management of adolescents, particularly concerning eating disorders."}{"title": "ISABEL M. CORNEJO-PAREJA:Isabel M. Cornejo-Pareja is a researcher and author associated with the study of intestinal microbiota and obesity."}{"title": "ARACELI MU\u00d1OZ-GARACH:Araceli Mu\u00f1oz-Garach is a researcher and author involved in the field of endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "FRANCISCO J. TINAHONES-MADUE\u00d1O:Francisco J. Tinahones-Madue\u00f1o is a researcher and author specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "J ADOLESCENT HEALTH:J Adolescent Health is a medical journal that publishes research and articles related to adolescent health issues, including eating disorders."}{"title": "RESTRICTIVE EATING DISORDERS:"}{"title": "PROYECTO DEL MICROBIOMA HUMANO:El Proyecto del Microbioma Humano es una iniciativa de investigaci\u00f3n a gran escala que estudia la diversidad y funcionalidad de la microbiota intestinal humana."}{"title": "META HIT:MetaHIT es un proyecto de investigaci\u00f3n que se centra en la caracterizaci\u00f3n de la microbiota intestinal y su relaci\u00f3n con la salud humana."}{"title": "LACTOBACILLUS:Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria that resides in the gastrointestinal tract and is widely recognized for its numerous health benefits, particularly in relation to digestive health. This genus is commonly utilized as probiotics, which are live microorganisms that confer health advantages when consumed in adequate amounts. Lactobacillus is known for its ability to ferment lactose and produce lactic acid, contributing to gut health and the maintenance of a positive metabolic profile.\n\nResearch has indicated that Lactobacillus may have beneficial effects on obesity and metabolic health, making it a subject of interest in studies related to these areas. Additionally, Lactobacillus can ferment undigested carbohydrates into D-lactic acid, which may lead to complications in certain patients, such as those with short bowel syndrome (SIC). The growth and activity of Lactobacillus can be enhanced by prebiotic fibers, further supporting its role in promoting gut health.\n\nOverall, Lactobacillus is a significant type of beneficial bacteria within the phylum Firmicutes, playing a crucial role in fermentation processes and contributing positively to digestive and metabolic health."}{"title": "STREPTOCOCCUS:Streptococcus is a genus of bacteria belonging to the phylum Firmicutes. These bacteria are commonly found in the gastrointestinal tract and play a significant role in human health and microbiota. Streptococcus can have both beneficial and pathogenic effects, highlighting its dual nature in the context of human health."}{"title": "BACTEROIDES:Bacteroides is a genus of bacteria that plays a crucial role in the human gut, particularly in the digestion of complex carbohydrates. It is predominantly found in the intestines and is part of the phylum Bacteroidetes. Research has shown that Bacteroides is negatively associated with obesity, suggesting that its presence may be linked to healthier weight management. Interestingly, this genus has also been found to increase in individuals who successfully lose weight. Additionally, Bacteroides is more prevalent in the intestinal microbiota of African children, which is associated with diets rich in plant fiber. Overall, Bacteroides is essential for digestive health and may influence body weight regulation."}{"title": "BACILLUS:Bacillus is a genus of bacteria that encompasses species significant for their roles in fermentation and intestinal health. These bacteria are recognized for their resilience and are utilized as probiotics, contributing to various health benefits."}{"title": "CLOSTRIDIUM:Clostridium is a genus of bacteria within the phylum Firmicutes, encompassing species that can be either beneficial or pathogenic in the human intestine. This genus has been associated with various health implications, including its role in gut health and disease. Notably, certain species of Clostridium have been linked to obesity and metabolic alterations, highlighting their impact on metabolic health. Overall, Clostridium plays a complex role in the human gut, contributing to both beneficial functions and potential pathogenic effects."}{"title": "FIRMICUTES:Firmicutes is a phylum of bacteria that plays a significant role in the human intestinal microbiota, particularly noted for its high prevalence in the gut microbiota of European children, where it is associated with diets rich in fats and animal proteins. This phylum is crucial for the fermentation of nutrients and has been linked to increased energy absorption, especially in obese individuals, where it tends to be found in higher proportions compared to the Bacteroidetes phylum. Research has indicated that the abundance of Firmicutes can change following antibiotic treatment and that it shows a proportional decrease in individuals after undergoing Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery. Overall, Firmicutes represents a substantial component of the gut microbiome, influencing metabolic processes and potentially contributing to obesity."}{"title": "BACTEROIDETES:Bacteroidetes is a phylum of bacteria that plays a crucial role in digestion and intestinal health. It is a significant component of the gut microbiota and is associated with lean body mass. Research indicates that individuals with obesity tend to have lower ratios of Bacteroidetes compared to Firmicutes, suggesting that this phylum is linked to reduced energy absorption. Additionally, Bacteroidetes is influenced by antibiotic treatment, as demonstrated in various studies. Overall, Bacteroidetes is essential for maintaining a healthy gut environment and may have implications for body weight regulation."}{"title": "ACTINOBACTERIAS:Actinobacterias es un filo de bacterias que incluye especies que son parte de la microbiota intestinal y tienen funciones metab\u00f3licas importantes."}{"title": "TRACTO GASTROINTESTINAL:El tracto gastrointestinal es el sistema de \u00f3rganos que se encarga de la digesti\u00f3n y absorci\u00f3n de nutrientes en el cuerpo humano."}{"title": "INTESTINO GRUESO:El intestino grueso es la parte del tracto gastrointestinal donde reside la mayor cantidad de bacterias y se lleva a cabo la absorci\u00f3n de agua y electrolitos."}{"title": "EST\u00d3MAGO:El est\u00f3mago es un \u00f3rgano del tracto gastrointestinal donde se inicia la digesti\u00f3n de los alimentos y alberga diversas bacterias, incluyendo Helicobacter pylori."}{"title": "DUODENO:The duodeno, or duodenum, is the first part of the small intestine, playing a crucial role in the digestive process. It is primarily responsible for the chemical digestion of food, aided by enzymes and bile. In addition to its digestive functions, the duodeno is significant for nutrient absorption, specifically calcium and copper. Furthermore, it is the site where the final digestion of carbohydrates occurs, highlighting its importance in the overall digestive system."}{"title": "PARTO NATURAL:Parto natural (natural birth) is associated with the newborn acquiring a microbiota similar to that of the mother's vaginal microbiota."}{"title": "LACTANCIA NATURAL:Lactancia natural (natural breastfeeding) is a key factor in the development of the newborn's intestinal microbiota, providing a continuous supply of beneficial bacteria."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N S\u00d3LIDA:Alimentaci\u00f3n s\u00f3lida (solid food introduction) marks a significant change in the composition of the intestinal microbiota as the child grows."}{"title": "DESTETE:Destete (weaning) is the process that further diversifies the intestinal microbiota as the child transitions to solid foods."}{"title": "ELDERMET:ELDERMET is a consortium that studies the microbiota of the elderly, finding distinct characteristics compared to younger adults."}{"title": "FILO: BACTEROIDETES:Filo: Bacteroidetes is another major phylum of bacteria that plays a crucial role in the composition of the intestinal microbiota."}{"title": "ENTEROBACTERIACEAE:Enterobacteriaceae is a family of bacteria within the phylum Proteobacteria, commonly found in the intestines and important for gut flora."}{"title": "ENTEROCOCCUS:Enterococcus is a genus of bacteria belonging to the phylum Firmicutes, commonly found in the intestines and playing a significant role in gut health. Notably, Enterococcus species, such as E. faecalis and E. faecium, are known to be involved in catheter-related infections, highlighting their clinical relevance in healthcare settings."}{"title": "VEILLONELLA:Veillonella is a genus of bacteria within the phylum Firmicutes, known for its role in the human microbiome."}{"title": "EUBACTERIUM:Eubacterium is a genus of bacteria that plays a significant role in metabolic health and obesity. It is part of the normal gut flora and is involved in various metabolic processes essential for maintaining gut health. Eubacterium belongs to the phylum Firmicutes, highlighting its importance in the overall functioning of the gastrointestinal system."}˝¬0␀␀␀␀␀º√0␀␀␀␀␀Zƒ0␀␀␀␀␀ƒ0␀␀␀␀␀ª∆0␀␀␀␀␀\«0␀␀␀␀␀˜«0␀␀␀␀␀ö»0␀␀␀␀␀u…0␀␀␀␀␀8 0␀␀␀␀␀SÃ0␀␀␀␀␀˜Ã0␀␀␀␀␀óÕ0␀␀␀␀␀NŒ0␀␀␀␀␀6—0␀␀␀␀␀„—0␀␀␀␀␀n“0␀␀␀␀␀”0␀␀␀␀␀•”0␀␀␀␀␀÷‘0␀␀␀␀␀o’0␀␀␀␀␀÷0␀␀␀␀␀÷0␀␀␀␀␀(◊0␀␀␀␀␀ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀›ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀O⁄0␀␀␀␀␀Æ‹0␀␀␀␀␀Û‡0␀␀␀␀␀∑·0␀␀␀␀␀Œ„0␀␀␀␀␀}‰0␀␀␀␀␀Ê0␀␀␀␀␀Á0␀␀␀␀␀óÁ0␀␀␀␀␀Ë0␀␀␀␀␀È0␀␀␀␀␀~Î0␀␀␀␀␀}Ì0␀␀␀␀␀(Ó0␀␀␀␀␀ÕÓ0␀␀␀␀␀hÔ0␀␀␀␀␀‰Ô0␀␀␀␀␀u0␀␀␀␀␀0␀␀␀␀␀uÚ0␀␀␀␀␀¸Ú0␀␀␀␀␀]Û0␀␀␀␀␀ Û0␀␀␀␀␀7ı0␀␀␀␀␀~ˆ0␀␀␀␀␀ù˜0␀␀␀␀␀‚¯0␀␀␀␀␀C˙0␀␀␀␀␀¥˙0␀␀␀␀␀˚0␀␀␀␀␀p˚0␀␀␀␀␀÷˚0␀␀␀␀␀p¸0␀␀␀␀␀◊¸0␀␀␀␀␀±ˇ0␀␀␀␀␀B␀1␀␀␀␀␀\1␀␀␀␀␀Ò1␀␀␀␀␀k1␀␀␀␀␀<1␀␀␀␀␀†1␀␀␀␀␀21␀␀␀␀␀Ï1␀␀␀␀␀±1␀␀␀␀␀R
